latest_plan = "Based on our reflection, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Analyze the input grid:\n   a. Identify the grid dimensions.\n   b. Locate all horizontal and vertical dividing lines (color 2 or 6).\n   c. Determine the sections created by these dividing lines.\n\n2. Create a deep copy of the input grid to modify.\n\n3. For each vertical section:\n   a. Determine the top and bottom boundaries of the section.\n   b. Calculate the middle row of the section.\n   \n   c. Analyze the pattern in the section:\n      - Count non-zero, non-dividing line cells in the top and bottom halves.\n      - Identify the unique colors present in each half.\n      - Determine which half has the more complex pattern based on cell count and color variety.\n\n   d. Apply mirroring:\n      - If one half is empty and the other contains a pattern:\n        * Mirror the non-empty half's pattern to the empty half.\n      - If both halves contain patterns:\n        * Mirror the more complex pattern to overwrite the less complex one.\n      - If both halves are empty, leave the section unchanged.\n\n   e. Mirroring process:\n      - For each row in the source half:\n        * Copy its pattern to the corresponding mirrored row in the target half.\n      - Ensure that patterns that extend beyond the middle are fully mirrored.\n\n4. Preserve the original dividing lines:\n   - Restore all cells with colors 2 or 6 to their original state.\n\n5. Handle edge cases:\n   - For sections with an odd number of rows, include the middle row in both halves during analysis and mirroring.\n   - Ensure that patterns touching dividing lines are correctly mirrored without altering the dividing lines.\n\n6. Verify the transformation:\n   - Check that all sections have been processed.\n   - Ensure that dividing lines remain intact.\n   - Confirm that patterns have been correctly mirrored within their sections.\n\n7. Return the transformed grid.\n\nThis plan addresses the key aspects of the challenge while taking into account the nuances we identified in our reflection. It provides a systematic approach to handle various scenarios, including complex patterns, multiple colors, and potential edge cases. The plan is designed to be general enough to handle a wide range of inputs while still adhering to the specific rules of the challenge."
